WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.408
Why long tasks fail.

2
00:00:01.688 --> 00:00:19.587
Chip Huyen’s essay on agents (January 2025) gives the arithmetic that should make you cautious: if each step is right 95% of the time and steps fail independently, ten steps succeed together only about 60% of the time, and a hundred steps almost never.

3
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:26.181
Real agents can do better than that because they observe results and correct course, but the direction is right.

4
00:00:26.461 --> 00:00:29.448
Errors compound, and long tasks need checkpoints.

5
00:00:29.728 --> 00:00:41.376
Her essay also lists the failure modes worth logging, which you will use in Studio 3 style error analysis of agent traces: Invalid tool: calling a tool that does not exist.

6
00:00:41.656 --> 00:00:46.157
Invalid parameters: the right tool with missing or malformed arguments.

7
00:00:46.437 --> 00:00:51.813
Incorrect values: well-formed arguments that are wrong, such as the wrong customer id.

8
00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:56.211
Goal failure: ignoring a constraint such as a budget or a deadline.

9
00:00:56.491 --> 00:01:00.245
False completion: the agent believes it is done when it is not.

10
00:01:00.525 --> 00:01:05.517
Her example is assigning 40 of 50 people to rooms and reporting success.

11
00:01:05.797 --> 00:01:14.309
Anthropic’s November 2025 post on harnesses for long-running agents reports the same patterns in a coding setting.

12
00:01:14.589 --> 00:01:23.848
Agents tried to do too much at once (one-shotting) and ran out of context mid-feature, and later sessions saw partial progress and declared the job finished.

13
00:01:24.128 --> 00:01:35.776
Their fixes were structural, not clever prompts: a feature list that defines the full scope, one feature at a time, and a rule that a feature is marked passing only after it is tested end to end.

14
00:01:36.056 --> 00:01:40.109
The lesson for your harness: success has to be checked, not reported.

15
00:01:40.389 --> 00:01:44.123
“The model said it’s done” is a stop reason, not a verification.
